1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,100
我是杰森.西弗，是个心理医生
Hi. I'm Jason Seaver. I'm a psychiatrist.

2
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:07,220
过去15年里 我致力于解决患者的问题
I've spent the last 15 years helping people with their problems.

3
00:00:07,236 --> 00:00:08,704
我是麦姬.西弗
And I'm Maggie Seaver.

4
00:00:08,940 --> 00:00:10,940
过去15年里，我一直围着孩子们转
I've spent the last 15 years helping our kids...

5
00:00:10,940 --> 00:00:13,140
解决那些杰森也束手无策的问题
with problems even Jason wouldn't believe.

6
00:00:13,420 --> 00:00:16,880
现在麦姬已重操旧业 在一家当地报社做记者
Now Maggie has gone back to work as a reporter for the local newspaper.

7
00:00:17,080 --> 00:00:20,540
杰森把他的诊所搬到了家里 这样就可以陪着孩子们了
And Jason has moved his practice into the house so we can be there for the kids.

8
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:22,680
-他们是可爱的孩子 -大多时候都是
- They're great kids. - Most of the time.

9
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:24,040
但是有时…
And the rest of the time....

10
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:26,980
-但是我们爱他们 -是的
- We love them, anyway. - Yeah.

11
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:28,320
鬼才相信
Unbelievable.

12
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:38,000
(English Subtitle) Growing.Pains.S01E02 -= Springsteen =- Subripped by zerox

13
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:36,060
斯普林斯丁的演唱会门票终于来了
This is it, my Springsteen tickets.

14
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:37,060
喂
Hello?

15
00:01:38,660 --> 00:01:39,980
他们什么时候才会讨厌溜冰板？
When do they outgrow skateboards?

16
00:01:40,360 --> 00:01:41,700
等你送他们架相机后
When you buy them a Camaro.

17
00:01:43,540 --> 00:01:45,740
对，好的
Yeah, okay.

18
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:47,300
拜
Bye.

19
00:01:48,700 --> 00:01:50,320
要去听演唱会了是吗？
Gonna see Springsteen, huh?

20
00:01:50,760 --> 00:01:53,360
对，明天晚上，肯定很精彩
Yep. Tomorrow night. It's gonna be awesome.

21
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:55,440
女士们先生们…
Ladies and gentlemen...

22
00:01:57,160 --> 00:01:58,300
演出开始
the Boss.

23
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:05,680
我还以为演唱会的票 一早卖光了呢
Wait, wait. I thought the Springsteen concert was sold-out.

24
00:02:06,320 --> 00:02:07,000
卖光了？
Sold-out?

25
00:02:10,060 --> 00:02:13,040
凯罗，对门路多的人来说 什么买不到？
Carol, to a man with connections, nothing is ever sold-out.

26
00:02:14,120 --> 00:02:16,440
刚才打电话来的是塞斯.詹姆森
That just happened to be Seth Jameson...

27
00:02:16,440 --> 00:02:19,520
他叔叔的小舅子在体育馆里面…
nephew of the man whose brother-in-law owns a hot-dog concession...

28
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:20,340
有个卖小吃的摊位
at the Coliseum.

29
00:02:21,120 --> 00:02:21,680
哇哦
Wow.

30
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:24,240
那你弄到票没？
So did you get tickets?

31
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:28,420
弄到票没？当然弄到啦
Did I get tickets? Of course l got tickets.

32
00:02:28,840 --> 00:02:30,800
是吗？斯普林斯丁演唱会的门票？
You did? To Springsteen?

33
00:02:31,020 --> 00:02:32,380
不
Well, no.

34
00:02:32,982 --> 00:02:34,609
去喝冰酸梅汤…
To the Ice Capades...

35
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:38,020
那的座位很舒服
but I got very good seats...

36
00:02:38,780 --> 00:02:40,080
还免费送两个热狗
and two free hot dogs.

37
00:02:42,700 --> 00:02:46,380
讲到门路关系 那么热狗是纯牛肉的吗？
Talk about connections. Are those all-beef dogs?

38
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:49,840
音乐会的门票那么难搞 你一定很失望吧
It's too bad about the concert, honey. You must be disappointed.

39
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:53,000
不，办法有的是，票我准能弄到
No, I actually got a couple of other things going. Ill get the tickets.

40
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:55,700
你们看，办法来了
All right. This is it.

41
00:02:56,460 --> 00:02:57,060
喂？
Hello?

42
00:02:58,200 --> 00:02:59,200
对，你说吧
Yeah. Talk to me.

43
00:03:01,220 --> 00:03:01,820
是的
Yeah.

44
00:03:04,220 --> 00:03:04,820
Yeah.

45
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:05,920
好吧
Okay.

46
00:03:06,882 --> 00:03:08,419
回头再说
Yeah, Ill see you.

47
00:03:09,760 --> 00:03:10,780
又没戏？
No dice?

48
00:03:11,340 --> 00:03:14,980
杰里说他朋友蛐蛐儿准能 帮我们弄到票的…
No. Jerry was sure he'd be able to get those tickets from his friend Cheech, but--

49
00:03:14,980 --> 00:03:15,440
蛐蛐儿？
Cheech?

50
00:03:16,020 --> 00:03:18,240
杰森，他竟然认识个叫蛐蛐儿的人
Jason, our son knows people named Cheech?

51
00:03:19,100 --> 00:03:22,060
麦姬，怎么能凭名字来判断一个人呢
Maggie, you cant judge somebody on the basis of a name.

52
00:03:22,660 --> 00:03:23,960
麦克，你往下说
Anyway, Mike, you were saying?

53
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:27,700
蛐蛐儿都快被判刑了 可他还在倒卖票子
Yeah, well, Cheech's parole officer didn't think it'd be such a good idea for him...

54
00:03:27,936 --> 00:03:30,302
蛐蛐儿的假释监护人认为这样不好
to be scalping tickets so close to the trial.

55
00:03:31,660 --> 00:03:33,320
你可真有眼力，蛐蛐儿
Good judgment, there, Cheech.

56
00:03:33,575 --> 00:03:35,008
太遗憾了，宝贝
Were sorry, honey.

57
00:03:35,640 --> 00:03:36,380
没关系
That's all right.

58
00:03:37,140 --> 00:03:40,180
办法嘛，我总会有的
I still got one more shot.

59
00:03:43,018 --> 00:03:46,455
小吉，我是麦克
Hey, Jimski. Yeah, it's Mike.

60
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:50,120
听我说，我一定要搞到一张票子
Yeah. Look, I gotta have those tickets.

61
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:53,400
对，他想要什么都可以
Yes. Look, offer them anything they want.

62
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:54,740
什么？
What?

63
00:03:55,860 --> 00:03:56,860
我的夹克衫
My jacket?

64
00:03:57,580 --> 00:04:00,780
我的皮夹克？ 真正小牛皮做的那件夹克？
My leather jacket? The one that smells like actual cattle?

65
00:04:02,260 --> 00:04:06,440
他送了两年的报纸才买了那件夹克 他喜欢那件衣服
He delivered papers for two years to get that jacket. He loves that jacket.

66
00:04:06,860 --> 00:04:07,980
连我都喜欢
I love that jacket.

67
00:04:08,460 --> 00:04:10,480
这么高级的衣服我都没穿过
Of course, I never had a jacket that nice.

68
00:04:11,613 --> 00:04:13,582
好吧，夹克衫可以给他
Okay, okay, he can have the jacket.

69
00:04:14,460 --> 00:04:16,800
拜托啦，吉米…
Oh, come on. Jimmy....

70
00:04:19,922 --> 00:04:22,357
这话我很难跟杰里说出口的
Look, I hate to even ask Jerry that.

71
00:04:25,320 --> 00:04:27,760
好吧，我等你电话
Yeah, all right. Look, call me right back.

72
00:04:32,334 --> 00:04:34,598
他们想跟杰里的妹妹约会
He wanted a date with Jerry's sister.

73
00:04:35,400 --> 00:04:35,820
翠茜？
Trixie?

74
00:04:36,820 --> 00:04:37,900
她才11岁啊
She's only 11.

75
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:39,440
我说了不行
I said no.

76
00:04:42,220 --> 00:04:45,100
麦克，那件夹克衫你真的愿、意让出去？
Say, Mike, you don't really want to part with that jacket, do you?

77
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:47,900
不，可是爸爸，这场演唱会…
No, but, Dad, there's no way that Bruce...

78
00:04:47,900 --> 00:04:50,920
就在我们家不远的地方举办 我不想错过
is gonna play 10 miles from my house, and I'm gonna miss him.

79
00:04:51,160 --> 00:04:52,220
我一定要去听一场
Dad, I gotta go to that concert.

80
00:04:53,320 --> 00:04:55,280
-又来了 -喂
- There it is. - Yep.

81
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,140
什么？
What?

82
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:00,460
这怎么行呢
That's impossible.

83
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:04,940
是的
Yeah.

84
00:05:05,767 --> 00:05:08,338
好吧，再见
Okay. See you.

85
00:05:09,360 --> 00:05:09,780
怎么了？
Well?

86
00:05:10,400 --> 00:05:12,780
-有人用房子换票子 -用房子？
- Somebody offered him a house. - A house?

87
00:05:13,008 --> 00:05:17,411
对，他们想度个周末 可我们办不到
Well, it was just for a weekend, but that's still out of our league.

88
00:05:24,180 --> 00:05:25,180
-除非… -麦克
- Unless.... - Mike.

89
00:05:27,900 --> 00:05:29,020
好吧，那算了
Okay. Fine.

90
00:05:29,958 --> 00:05:33,690
麦克，这至少能保住那件夹克对吗？
Hey, Mike, at least you still have that jacket, right?

91
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:36,540
管它呢，闻起来一股死牛味
Who cares? It smells like a dead cow.

92
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:43,980
妈妈…我看见楼上有只大老鼠
Mom, Mom, Mom. I just saw a mouse in the attic this big.

93
00:05:44,706 --> 00:05:47,004
它究竟是老鼠还是小羊？
Was this a mouse or a small sheep?

94
00:05:47,500 --> 00:05:51,640
它长着贼溜溜的眼睛 长尾巴，走起路来就像这样
Well, it had beady little eyes and a long tail, and went like this.

95
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:55,960
那是羊，没错
That's a sheep, all right.

96
00:05:56,660 --> 00:05:58,980
好吧，我的老鼠夹放哪去了？
Okay, okay. Where did I put those mousetraps?

97
00:05:59,860 --> 00:06:01,900
你找老鼠夹干嘛，妈妈？
What are you gonna do with the mousetraps, Mom?

98
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:05,900
老实跟你说吧，凯罗 我打算用它来夹老鼠
Well, Ill be honest with you, Carol, I plan to use them to trap mice.

99
00:06:06,395 --> 00:06:08,796
-会把老鼠夹死吗？ -但愿、如此
- Wont that kill them? - Hopefully.

100
00:06:09,140 --> 00:06:09,660
妈妈
Mom.

101
00:06:10,920 --> 00:06:15,060
凯罗，当妈的就该做好 自己的份内事
Carol, a mom's gotta do what a mom's gotta do.

102
00:06:15,580 --> 00:06:17,520
儿子，把奶酪给我拿来
Son, bring me my Camembert.

103
00:06:17,860 --> 00:06:20,380
好极了，老鼠一定会上钩的
All right. Were going with the big guns.

104
00:06:22,444 --> 00:06:26,449
妈妈，老鼠是个聪明无害的动物啊
Well, Mom, I mean, they're cute, harmless little creatures.

105
00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:29,620
凯罗，十世纪的时候，就是老鼠…
Carol, these are the same guys who carried the plague all through Europe...

106
00:06:29,620 --> 00:06:31,760
让瘟疫传遍整个欧洲 害死了数千万人
during the 10th century and killed millions of people.

107
00:06:32,387 --> 00:06:34,516
那是一千年前的事了，妈妈
That was 1,000 years ago, Mom.

108
00:06:34,640 --> 00:06:36,420
你难道还不能原谅它吗？
How long are you going to hold a grudge?

109
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:45,660
麦克
Michael.

110
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,200
来吧
Go ahead. Try it.

111
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:51,160
你帮我想一个活下去的理由吧，妈妈
Try to give me one good reason to go on living, Mom.

112
00:06:52,900 --> 00:06:54,800
来个摇滚歌星舞会
The Solid Gold dancers.

113
00:06:59,081 --> 00:07:00,810
可惜爸爸不在家
Well, at least Dads not here.

114
00:07:01,040 --> 00:07:03,600
他倒是会帮我驱散我的烦恼
I mean, he'd really try to cheer me up.

115
00:07:04,200 --> 00:07:05,280
他是个滑头
The slime.

116
00:07:06,380 --> 00:07:10,040
他装得好像一直都很同情我
I mean, he always acts like he's gonna be real sympathetic...

117
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:12,520
然后他会一下子跟你说…
and then before you know it, he turns on you:

118
00:07:13,340 --> 00:07:14,960
“麦克…”
"Mike, Mike, Mike.

119
00:07:16,265 --> 00:07:18,336
“我认为在这种情况下…”
"l find that at times like these...

120
00:07:18,460 --> 00:07:20,880
“对生活你最好还是要往前看”
"it's always best to keep a little perspective on life."

121
00:07:25,220 --> 00:07:26,500
至少他从没对你说过…
At least he didn't give you that line...

122
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:28,640
他像你这么大时有什么苦闷
about how rough he had it when he was your age.

123
00:07:29,500 --> 00:07:32,280
确实没有，他常说…
No, no. That's right. He always says:

124
00:07:34,340 --> 00:07:34,860
“麦克…”
"Mike...

125
00:07:35,584 --> 00:07:39,120
“我不想跟你谈我在你这么大时 有多么苦闷…”
"lm not gonna give you that line about how rough I had it when l was your age...

126
00:07:39,120 --> 00:07:41,280
“但你要知道从历史上来看…”
"but I think that you should be aware...

127
00:07:41,280 --> 00:07:43,960
“比你苦闷的人多着呢”
"that historically, people have had it rougher than this."

128
00:07:45,940 --> 00:07:47,380
-嗨 -嗨
- Hi. - Hi.

129
00:07:48,220 --> 00:07:49,220
家里有老鼠吗？
Do we have mice?

130
00:07:50,080 --> 00:07:50,540
是的
Yep...

131
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:54,140
如果我24小时还不回来…
and if I'm not back in 24 hours...

132
00:07:56,660 --> 00:07:57,440
你就买只猫吧
call a cat.

133
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:03,720
麦克…
Mike, Mike, Mike.

134
00:08:07,100 --> 00:08:08,700
情绪仍然不好吗，小伙子？
Still feeling pretty low, huh, pal?

135
00:08:09,918 --> 00:08:12,456
我很好，老爸 别谈这个，好吗？
Dad, I'm feeling fine. Let's just drop it, okay?

136
00:08:12,620 --> 00:08:14,800
别这样嘛，我明白你现在的心情
Come on, come on. I know what you're going through.

137
00:08:15,560 --> 00:08:17,720
-那当然 -我真的明白
- Yeah, sure, Dad. - No, I do. l really do.

138
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:20,540
今早怕你不开心，所以我才没说
You know, I didn't want to bring it up this morning and depress you...

139
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:24,820
我听过斯普林斯丁的演唱会
but I have seen Springsteen in concert.

140
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:25,880
你听过？
You have?

141
00:08:27,080 --> 00:08:28,260
十年前吧
Ten years ago.

142
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,360
-是吗？感觉如何？ -棒极了
- Really? What was it like? - Amazing.

143
00:08:32,020 --> 00:08:34,720
他的音乐简直能把门都震破
I mean, the guy completely blows your doors off.

144
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:37,279
-够了，我不想听这个 -他简直让我…
- God, I don't want to hear this. - He made me feel so...

145
00:08:37,279 --> 00:08:39,077
-行了，老爸 -解脱
- Please, Dad. - ... free.

146
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:40,849
当时我走出演唱会现场…
I could have just walked out of that concert...

147
00:08:40,849 --> 00:08:42,720
差点能搭便车周游全国
and hitchhiked right across country.

148
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:43,920
-别说了 -对不起
- Stop! - Sorry.

149
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:48,820
麦克，如果让你许一个愿、望…
Mike, if you had one wish right now...

150
00:08:50,160 --> 00:08:51,340
你最想要什么？
one thing, what would it be?

151
00:08:51,560 --> 00:08:53,720
爸爸，我现在没这个心情
Dad, I'm really not in the mood for this.

152
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:55,360
别这样，麦克 说来听听嘛
Come on, Mike. Come on, come on, come on.

153
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:57,520
如果让你许个愿、望…
I mean, if you had one thing...

154
00:08:57,520 --> 00:08:59,700
一个能让你感到万分幸福的愿、望 你会想要什么？
that would make you the happiest guy in the world, what would it be?

155
00:09:02,740 --> 00:09:04,180
纯金舞者
A Solid Gold dancer.

156
00:09:05,620 --> 00:09:06,760
好吧，让你许两个愿、望
All right, two wishes.

157
00:09:09,220 --> 00:09:11,160
要一张演唱会的前排票子
Front-row tickets to the Springsteen concert.

158
00:09:14,416 --> 00:09:17,380
第7排的可以吗？
Well, would seventh-row be all right?

159
00:09:17,380 --> 00:09:19,700
爸爸，你就别玩弄我的感情了
Come on, Dad. don't toy with my emotions.

160
00:09:25,380 --> 00:09:29,660
亨廷顿干洗店，三件亲衫 洗净熨平不要上奖
"Huntington Dry Cleaning. Three shirts, clean, press, no starch."

161
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:32,200
谢谢爸爸 这是我第三个愿、望
Thanks, Dad. That was my third wish.

162
00:09:34,160 --> 00:09:36,060
好吧，是我搞错了
Okay, okay. Sorry. Wrong pocket.

163
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:38,060
这张怎样？
How about these?

164
00:09:48,083 --> 00:09:49,653
天哪
It cant be.

165
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,040
爸爸，你知道这是什么吗？
Dad, do you know what these are?

166
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:53,860
-斯普林斯丁的演唱会门票! -真的？
- These are Springsteen tickets! - Really?

167
00:09:54,489 --> 00:09:56,924
真不敢相信，你怎么弄到的？
I cant believe it. How did you get them?

168
00:09:56,960 --> 00:09:58,940
我今天和你妈作了个决定
Well, Mike, your mom and I made a big decision.

169
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:02,480
要么花钱让你念大学 要么拿来买这些票子
We could either afford to send you to college or we could get those tickets.

170
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:06,180
-你觉得怎样？ -你选择得太对了
- What do you think? - I think you made the right choice.

171
00:10:07,060 --> 00:10:09,620
太棒了，两张演唱会的票子
I cant believe it. Two tickets to Springsteen.

172
00:10:10,405 --> 00:10:13,240
杰里知道的话肯定会发疯的
Wait till I call Jerry. He's gonna freak.

173
00:10:13,240 --> 00:10:15,220
等一下，可怜可怜他吧
Hey, wait a minute. Show some compassion.

174
00:10:16,380 --> 00:10:18,500
杰里知道我们去看的话 肯定会气死的
When Jerry finds out we're going, it's gonna kill him.

175
00:10:21,620 --> 00:10:23,220
不必再刺激人家啦
We don't want to rub it in.

176
00:10:26,320 --> 00:10:27,740
没错…
Right, right.

177
00:10:28,900 --> 00:10:32,120
麦克，你不介意和爸爸一起 去看演唱会吧？
Hey, Mike, you don't really mind going to the concert with your old man?

178
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:34,540
不…
No. No.

179
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:35,600
真的吗？
You sure?

180
00:10:36,020 --> 00:10:37,560
是的，这简直棒极了
Yeah. Dad, this is going to be great.

181
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,360
你不想跟你的哥们一起去吗？
I mean, you don't want to take one of your buddies?

182
00:10:39,780 --> 00:10:40,200
不
No.

183
00:10:40,900 --> 00:10:43,000
-想带杰里去吗？ -不
- You want to take Jerry? - No.

184
00:10:43,638 --> 00:10:46,320
-佩姬.泽琳斯基呢？ -不
- Peggy Zelinsky? - No.

185
00:10:46,320 --> 00:10:47,940
爸爸，我想和你去，真的
No, Dad, I want to go with you, really.

186
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:51,060
好啊，咱们打电话去气气杰里
Well, all right, then. Lets call Jerry and rub it in.

187
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:53,300
开个玩笑
Just kidding.

188
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:05,560
我发誓，哥们，我已经想尽办法了 但就是搞不到票
I swear it, man. I have tried everywhere. There is not one more ticket around.

189
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:07,060
麦克，你弄到票了吗？
Hey, Seaver, did you score tickets?

190
00:11:07,662 --> 00:11:10,028
我有说过要去弄票吗？
Hey, did I say I was gonna score the tickets?

191
00:11:11,040 --> 00:11:11,560
瞧这个
Voila.

192
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:15,860
太棒了，哥们 你从哪搞来的票？
Outrageous, man! Where did you get these?

193
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,840
我自有门路
I have my connections.

194
00:11:18,480 --> 00:11:21,810
小迈，伙计，好哥们
So, Mikey. Buddy. Broski.

195
00:11:21,810 --> 00:11:24,575
你弄到了多少张票？
Just how many tickets you got here?

196
00:11:24,746 --> 00:11:26,047
就两张
Just two.

197
00:11:26,047 --> 00:11:28,183
你以为他会带上你吗？靠边站吧
What? You think hes gonna take you, bonehead?

198
00:11:28,183 --> 00:11:30,345
你会带我去的，对吧，麦克？
Hes gonna take me, right, Mikey?

199
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:32,660
恕我爱莫能助了，哥们
Sorry, guys. No can do.

200
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:36,120
好吧，我能理解 你肯定是请…
Okay. Okay, I can respect that. Now let me guess.

201
00:11:37,220 --> 00:11:38,160
佩姬.泽琳斯基去，对吗？
Peggy Zelinsky, right?

202
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:40,400
伙计，这可是个好机会哦
Oh, man, what an opportunity.

203
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:43,660
你见过女孩子看完 演唱会后的样子吗？
Have you ever seen a girl after a Springsteen concert?

204
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:46,120
她们全变成了疯狂野兽
They turn into wild animals.

205
00:11:49,020 --> 00:11:52,140
-你邀请她了吗？ -还没有
- Have you asked her, yet? - Well, no, not exactly.

206
00:11:52,200 --> 00:11:56,440
佩姬喜欢我，但她对我没吸引力
I mean, Peggy wants me, man, but she just doesn't do it for me.

207
00:11:57,700 --> 00:12:00,440
我的英语要迟到了 先走一步
Look, I'm gonna be late for English. Gotta go.

208
00:12:00,549 --> 00:12:02,517
“我的英语要迟到了”
"lm gonna be late for English. Gotta go."

209
00:12:02,760 --> 00:12:04,540
麦克，你的英语也太烂了
Come on, Seaver, you barely speak English.

210
00:12:05,200 --> 00:12:06,460
你究竟要带谁去？
Who are you going with, man?

211
00:12:09,591 --> 00:12:10,659
“沃巴巴”
Mafuther.

212
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:11,320
谁？
What?

213
00:12:13,061 --> 00:12:15,564
-“沃巴巴” -沃巴巴是谁？
- Mafuther. - Who's Mafuther?

214
00:12:15,620 --> 00:12:17,360
是不是那个新来的巴基斯坦同学？
Wait. Is that that new weird kid from Pakistan?

215
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:20,820
不，我是和我老爸一起去
No, man. I'm going with my father.

216
00:12:23,772 --> 00:12:26,673
你要和你老爸去看演唱会？
You're gonna go see Springsteen with your father, man?

217
00:12:26,808 --> 00:12:29,678
我老爸可不像一般的父亲
Hey, look, my fathers not like a father, okay?

218
00:12:29,678 --> 00:12:31,111
他可是个很前卫的人
Hes a cool guy.

219
00:12:31,400 --> 00:12:34,240
是很前卫，上次我去他家时…
Yeah, hes cool. Last time I was over there...

220
00:12:34,280 --> 00:12:36,580
他爸正边给地板打蜡 嘴里边哼着<赶走龙王>
he was waxing the floor and singing Puff the Magic Dragon.

221
00:12:36,940 --> 00:12:38,480
别在这里胡说，波纳
don't be a jerk, all right, Boner?

222
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,340
老实说，麦克 这样太奇怪了
I'm telling you, Seaver, it's weird.

223
00:12:40,960 --> 00:12:42,120
有什么好奇怪的？
Look, it's not weird, okay?

224
00:12:42,880 --> 00:12:45,080
你不和自己老爸出去 是你自己傻冒
Just because you're too big a jerk to do anything with your father...

225
00:12:45,080 --> 00:12:47,160
这并不代表我这样做不正常
doesn't mean there's anything weird or un-cool about it.

226
00:12:47,896 --> 00:12:50,968
再说三道四我就要你们的命
You guys breathe a word of this to anybody and you're dead meat.

227
00:12:57,539 --> 00:12:59,641
★你开不了手中枪
You can't start a fire

228
00:12:59,641 --> 00:13:02,911
★不扣扳机你开不了手中枪
You can't start a fire without a spark

229
00:13:02,911 --> 00:13:04,412
★这支枪专供出租
This gun's for hire

230
00:13:04,412 --> 00:13:07,816
今晚最有趣的是 观众群里有各种年龄段的人
One fascinating aspect of tonight's crowd is its broad age range...

231
00:13:07,816 --> 00:13:09,284
如果我没猜错的话…
and if I'm not mistaken...

232
00:13:09,284 --> 00:13:12,879
今晚的演唱会 吸引了好几代观众前来
evidence of this cross-generational appeal is right here.

233
00:13:13,021 --> 00:13:15,218
请问一下，年轻人
Excuse me, young man.

234
00:13:15,624 --> 00:13:18,491
你是和你父亲来看演唱会的吗？
Did you attend this evenings concert with your father?

235
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:20,900
有谁会关心？
Who wants to know?

236
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:24,460
亲爱的观众朋友 这里是纽约新闻节目
All of the Tri-State area. This is Newsline New York.

237
00:13:27,900 --> 00:13:30,720
-先生，他是你儿子吗？ -这个大小伙子？
- Sir, is this your son? - Hey! The big fellow here?

238
00:13:30,740 --> 00:13:33,040
他不仅是我儿子 还是我最好的朋友
Not only is this my son, this is my best buddy.

239
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:37,260
你认为父子一起来 听摇滚乐演唱会…
Tell me, sir, isn't it unusual for a father and a son...

240
00:13:37,260 --> 00:13:39,280
是否是件不寻常的事情？
to attend a rock "n" roll concert together?

241
00:13:39,560 --> 00:13:41,420
当然不是，在我们家很正常
No, no way. No, not in our family.

242
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:43,480
我们彼此有着深厚的感情，对吗？
Not in any family that loves each other. Right?

243
00:13:47,155 --> 00:13:49,853
布鲁斯…我们爱死他了
Bruce, Bruce. We loved it.

244
00:13:50,600 --> 00:13:53,420
年轻人，你想和你的同学说几句吗？
Young man, anything you'd like to say to your friends at school?

245
00:14:06,660 --> 00:14:09,000
凯罗，我刚才到阁楼去了
Carol, I was just upstairs in the attic.

246
00:14:09,960 --> 00:14:11,560
太棒了，妈妈
Hey, that's great, Mom.

247
00:14:12,640 --> 00:14:17,480
奶酪没有了，捕鼠夹也闭上了 但却没有老鼠的影子
All the cheese is gone and all the traps are sprung, but there's no mice in them.

248
00:14:17,480 --> 00:14:18,800
是吗？
Really?

249
00:14:19,540 --> 00:14:22,940
凯罗，我和老鼠并没有私人来恩怨
Carol, I have nothing personal against these mice.

250
00:14:23,320 --> 00:14:26,500
但我孩子们的健康要比老鼠更重要
It's just that my children's health is more important to me than theirs is.

251
00:14:28,340 --> 00:14:28,860
好吧
Fine!

252
00:14:30,300 --> 00:14:31,880
你尽管杀光它们吧…
Just go ahead and kill them...

253
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,280
但什么时候是个头呢，妈妈？
but where does it stop, Mom?

254
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:38,220
今天是老鼠 明天是邻居家狂叫的狗…
Today it's mice, tomorrow it's the neighbors barking dog...

255
00:14:39,440 --> 00:14:43,180
说不定哪天就轮到邮递员了
then maybe the mailman's late one day.

256
00:14:46,181 --> 00:14:49,583
杀害邮递员可是件人命案，妈妈
Killing a mailman is a federal offense, Mom.

257
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:53,720
她的反应还不算过激
Well, at least she didn't overreact.

258
00:14:56,040 --> 00:14:58,560
麦克，演唱会…
Hey, Mike. How was the...

259
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:01,860
怎么样了？
concert?

260
00:15:03,640 --> 00:15:06,720
孩子们今天怎么都气乎乎的？
Is there an irate children's convention upstairs?

261
00:15:08,780 --> 00:15:09,360
怎么了？
What?

262
00:15:10,160 --> 00:15:11,420
麦克怎么了？
What's with Mike?

263
00:15:11,420 --> 00:15:13,420
我怎么知道？
How should I know?

264
00:15:15,340 --> 00:15:17,780
回来的路上他一句话也不说
Didn't say a word to me all the way home.

265
00:15:18,300 --> 00:15:18,820
Oh?

266
00:15:20,100 --> 00:15:22,860
也许是他觉得我让他出洋相了
I guess he thinks I embarrassed him or something.

267
00:15:24,260 --> 00:15:26,020
为什么？你干什么了？
Why? What did you do?

268
00:15:26,100 --> 00:15:28,520
我什么也没干 他反应过敏而已
I didn't do anything. He's overreacting.

269
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:33,680
刚才看完演唱会时 电视台采访我们…
We got interviewed by a television crew down there, and....

270
00:15:36,300 --> 00:15:37,080
算了
Never mind.

271
00:15:38,300 --> 00:15:40,720
我不想再谈了
I'd really rather not talk about it.

272
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:44,740
事情总会过去的…
Oh, well, I'm sure it'll blow over...

273
00:15:47,275 --> 00:15:48,674
明天之前…
by tomorrow...

274
00:15:50,712 --> 00:15:52,475
要么就后天
or the next day.

275
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,940
你好啊，电视大明星
So, how's my brother, the big TV star?

276
00:15:57,540 --> 00:15:59,820
别说了，凯罗 我今天倒霉透了
Hey, knock it off, Carol. I've been getting that all day.

277
00:16:00,260 --> 00:16:03,324
大家好，这里是纽约新闻
Hello, everybody, this is Newsline New York.

278
00:16:03,324 --> 00:16:06,362
在我身旁的是麦克和简森 这两个非常有趣的父子
Were here with Mike and Jason Seaver, two really cool guys.

279
00:16:06,594 --> 00:16:09,780
南茜星期六不肯和我去看电影 知道我怎么做的吗？
Nancy wouldn't go with me to the movies Saturday, so you know what I did?

280
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:11,880
-怎样？ -我叫了我老爸去看
- What? - I asked my dad.

281
00:16:13,260 --> 00:16:15,460
波纳，这没什么好乐的
Hey, Boner, you're a real funny guy.

282
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,420
小迈，听我说…
Hey, Mikey, listen.

283
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:20,660
你跟你爸，我跟我爸 来次双档怎么样？
Maybe you and your dad could double with me and my dad some night.

284
00:16:22,240 --> 00:16:23,760
小迈，跟我们说说…
Mikey, you can tell us.

285
00:16:24,080 --> 00:16:26,300
约会有进展吗？ 还只是跟人家道了声晚安？
Did you get lucky, or was that good night kiss all you got?

286
00:16:27,540 --> 00:16:30,200
你俩把脑叶切除后 果然变得有趣了
You guys are a lot funnier since your lobotomies.

287
00:16:33,240 --> 00:16:34,500
瞧这一家子
What a family.

288
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:38,080
儿子和老子约会 现在妹妹又站出来为哥哥辩护
The guy dates his dad, then gets his little sister to stick up for him.

289
00:16:38,100 --> 00:16:39,560
这到是件新鲜事哦
You know, this could make the news, too.

290
00:16:39,780 --> 00:16:42,840
我们是朋友，我爱死这小子了
What a guy. Were buddies. I love this guy!

291
00:16:58,060 --> 00:17:06,400
[救救老鼠] 快来，本
Come on, Ben.

292
00:17:07,220 --> 00:17:08,580
我需要你帮忙
I need your help.

293
00:17:10,060 --> 00:17:12,100
老鼠需要你的帮忙
The mice need your help.

294
00:17:12,427 --> 00:17:13,997
本人不过问政治
lm just not political.

295
00:17:15,460 --> 00:17:16,060
本…
Ben...

296
00:17:17,180 --> 00:17:21,060
现在有个原则问题 需要我们选择自己的立场
there comes a time when principle alone compels us to take a stand.

297
00:17:22,604 --> 00:17:24,220
-我给你两毛五 -一块
- Ill give you a quarter. - A dollar.

298
00:17:24,220 --> 00:17:25,800
-五毛 -救助老鼠
- Fifty cents. - Save the mice.

299
00:17:28,360 --> 00:17:32,040
救救老鼠，反对杀生
Save the mice. Release the rodents.

300
00:17:32,720 --> 00:17:36,020
好了，凯罗，你胜利了
Okay. Okay, Carol, I give up. You win.

301
00:17:36,551 --> 00:17:37,848
拿去吧
Here.

302
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,200
“平等自由的老鼠旅馆”
"Born Free Mouse Hotels.

303
00:17:43,940 --> 00:17:46,600
“老鼠进去之后，你要为它找到更合适的 生态环境它才会出来”
"Your mouse checks in and doesn't check out...

304
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,040
"until you find him a more suitable enviroment."

305
00:17:49,360 --> 00:17:50,780
还不止这些呢
And that's not all.

306
00:17:50,940 --> 00:17:53,500
简森，跟凯罗说说这些幸运的老鼠 赢得了什么
Jason, tell Carol what these lucky mice have won.

307
00:17:54,760 --> 00:17:57,980
麦姬，这些幸运老鼠 除了能保住性命之外…
Well, Maggie, in addition to having their lives spared...

308
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:01,360
还将受到全程护送 免费进行为期两周的休假
our furry little friends will be whisked away for a fun-filled, all-expense-paid...

309
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:04,160
地点是迪斯尼乐园
two-week vacation to Disneyland.

310
00:18:06,200 --> 00:18:10,240
它们将会在那里遇到老鼠之王 你们猜会是谁…
Yeah, where they will meet the big cheese himself, you guessed it:

311
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,180
就是米老鼠
Mickey Mouse.

312
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:14,380
别逗我了
You guys.

313
00:18:14,689 --> 00:18:16,157
嘿咻…
Boy, oh boy, oh boy.

314
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:18,520
就是说我们也去迪斯尼乐园？
Does this mean were going to Disneyland, too?

315
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:21,740
不
No.

316
00:18:27,380 --> 00:18:30,180
这么晚了，麦克上哪去了？
It's getting late. I wonder where Mike is.

317
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:32,740
你去图书馆找，我去博物馆找
You check the libraries. Ill check the museums.

318
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:37,600
真不明白他为什么这么小题大做
Why is he making such a federal case out of this?

319
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:40,600
昨晚一整晚不和我说话
You know, he didn't speak to me last night.

320
00:18:41,015 --> 00:18:44,452
今天又对我很冷淡 到现在还没回来
He gave me the cold shoulder this morning. Now hes two hours late.

321
00:18:44,700 --> 00:18:46,680
简森…
Jason, Jason, Jason.

322
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:52,220
我认为在目前的情况下 对生活你最好是朝前看
I find that at times like these, it's good to keep a little perspective on things.

323
00:18:53,640 --> 00:18:55,660
亲爱的，他现在的情绪肯定好转了
Honey, I'm sure he's over it by now.

324
00:18:59,160 --> 00:19:02,060
话说回来，我不是心理医生
On the other hand, I'm no psychiatrist.

325
00:19:02,580 --> 00:19:05,320
先失陪了 我得去安置那些小老鼠了
If you'll excuse me, I have to go tuck in the mice.

326
00:19:12,300 --> 00:19:14,520
这只鼻子很像你母亲
You did get your mothers nose.

327
00:19:18,380 --> 00:19:20,400
好吧，对不起 就当这是个傻玩笑吧
Okay, sorry, dumb joke.

328
00:19:20,855 --> 00:19:23,256
不，你的确是个 很风趣的人，爸爸
No, no. You're a laugh riot, Dad.

329
00:19:24,020 --> 00:19:24,980
麦克…
Hey, Mike...

330
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:29,440
对不起了，好吗？
I am sorry, okay?

331
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:31,640
我知道我让你难堪了，对不起
I know you feel I embarrassed you, and I'm sorry.

332
00:19:32,600 --> 00:19:34,760
-没什么，爸爸 -麦克…
- Yeah, sure. Great, Dad. - Mike...

333
00:19:36,304 --> 00:19:37,739
我向你道歉了
lm apologizing.

334
00:19:37,739 --> 00:19:40,777
难不成你还要我公开道歉吗？
don't you think we should get this out in the open?

335
00:19:40,800 --> 00:19:42,520
难道你想上国家电视台？
What, you mean like on national television?

336
00:19:44,720 --> 00:19:47,860
我花了很多钱才买到那两张票…
You know, I paid a lot of money for those tickets...

337
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:49,720
都是为了让你去看那场演唱会
and that was so you could go to the concert.

338
00:19:50,100 --> 00:19:52,160
我觉得你有点太顾着自己了…
I think you're being a little self-absorbed about--

339
00:19:52,253 --> 00:19:53,820
我太顾着自己？
lm being self-absorbed?

340
00:19:53,820 --> 00:19:56,380
爸，你在晚间新闻里让我出了洋相
Dad, you gave me noogies on the evening news.

341
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:02,240
有的父母把自己的儿女 关在家里长达7年
Well, some peoples parents lock them in a closet for seven years.

342
00:20:03,180 --> 00:20:06,780
你算好的了 有老爸这么疼你
You got it real rough. Your father likes you.

343
00:20:07,168 --> 00:20:08,863
还说什么难堪，出洋相
Gross, cooties!

344
00:20:10,200 --> 00:20:12,600
我当时是在表达我对你的情感，麦克
I was showing my feelings for you, Mike.

345
00:20:13,841 --> 00:20:15,810
你对妈妈也有情感…
You got feelings for Mom, too...

346
00:20:15,810 --> 00:20:19,212
难道你也会当着电视观众的面 表达出来？
but you don't go showing them in front of whole Tri-State area.

347
00:20:22,280 --> 00:20:27,120
爸，你不知道 我的那些同学…
Dad, you just don't know. I mean, the guys at school--

348
00:20:27,540 --> 00:20:29,900
行了，麦克 你那么在乎他们的话干嘛？
Come on, Mike, what do you care what those guys say?

349
00:20:30,940 --> 00:20:34,540
爸，你这话说得轻巧 你体会不到那种心情的
Dad, it's easy for you to say. You don't.... You just don't know what it's like.

350
00:20:35,100 --> 00:20:38,760
他们都在笑话我跟你一起出去
I mean, they laughed at me because I went with you...

351
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:43,400
我为你辩护 我说“我爸是个沉稳的人”
but I defended you. I said, "My dads a cool guy."

352
00:20:44,480 --> 00:20:45,520
而后你的表现呢？
And then what did you do?

353
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:47,780
你当众对我左亲右抱
You slobber all over me on Newsline New York.

354
00:20:49,760 --> 00:20:52,780
好吧，麦克，对不起
All right. Okay, Mike, I am sorry.

355
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:55,700
也许我们不该一起去看演唱会
Maybe we shouldn't have gone to the concert together.

356
00:20:56,284 --> 00:20:57,718
我不是这个意思
Hey, that's not what I'm saying.

357
00:20:57,718 --> 00:21:00,020
也许你该约个女孩一起去
No. I mean, maybe you just should have taken a girl.

358
00:21:00,020 --> 00:21:02,360
爸，你并没理解我
Dad, you're not listening to me.

359
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,220
Look...

360
00:21:07,595 --> 00:21:09,961
我说这话是冒着很大风险的
lm taking a big risk by telling you this...

361
00:21:12,200 --> 00:21:15,560
我是很喜欢和你一起去玩
but I actually like doing stuff with you.

362
00:21:16,180 --> 00:21:20,280
我想和自己老爸去看 斯普林斯丁的演唱会
I do. I mean, l was sitting there watching Springsteen with my dad...

363
00:21:20,340 --> 00:21:25,220
许多人的父母 连斯普林斯丁都不知道呢
and a lot of other people's parents don't even know what a Springsteen is.

364
00:21:26,540 --> 00:21:31,390
整个演唱会我一直在想 “这真是太棒了”
And all through the concert I was thinking, "Hey, you know, this is really great."

365
00:21:33,010 --> 00:21:33,610
就这样
Yeah.

366
00:21:34,110 --> 00:21:36,810
我当时的想法跟你差不多
Well, you know, I was thinking pretty much the same thing.

367
00:21:38,290 --> 00:21:41,990
也许我们都有一种共同的想法
Well, maybe there's a way that we can both think that...

368
00:21:42,650 --> 00:21:45,930
就是不想让外人来干扰这一切
without letting the entire free world in on it.

369
00:21:48,950 --> 00:21:52,750
我当时也许是有点失控了
Well, I guess l did lose control a little.

370
00:21:54,310 --> 00:21:55,410
是很失控
Okay, a lot.

371
00:21:57,290 --> 00:21:58,410
没关系了，爸爸
That's all right, Dad.

372
00:21:58,410 --> 00:22:01,330
摇滚乐是让人有点兴奋
I guess Bruce has that effect on people.

373
00:22:01,630 --> 00:22:05,530
也许我们下次就该听些 柔和点的音乐
I guess maybe next time we should see someone a little less dynamic.

374
00:22:06,710 --> 00:22:10,210
我听说“奥斯蒙兄弟”要来这里演出了
Well, I hear the Osmonds are coming to town.

375
00:22:25,770 --> 00:22:27,050
我爱死他了
I love this guy.

376
00:22:33,147 --> 00:22:36,914
告诉你们，看和听简直是两码事
You guys, I'm telling you, this does not compare with seeing him live.

377
00:22:40,821 --> 00:22:43,358
麦克…
Mike! Mike!

378
00:22:43,710 --> 00:22:47,170
你妈妈和我正在隔壁房间看书
Your mother and I are in the next room. Were trying to read.

379
00:22:48,150 --> 00:22:50,510
能不能把那玩意儿关小声点
You guys think you could turn down that....

380
00:22:52,370 --> 00:22:54,510
关小声点就是了
Turn down whoever that is.

381
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:55,000
